##
## Upstream tests to disable
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue.
##

# This test hardcodes kCommandExecuteImplClsid in a non-easily-replaceable way.
-LegacyCleanupsTest.Do

# This test hardcodes "GoogleUpdateIsMachine" in a non-easily-replaceable way,
# when we would need "BraveUpdateIsMachine".
-MiniInstallerConfigurationTest.IsSystemLevel

# This test fails on CI because it runs under Admin account: the failure is due
# to how the two SIDs are formatted, not because of the ACL.The test builds
# expected_dir_dacl from token.User().ToSddlString(), which gives the full SID
# (S-1-5-21-…-500). The actual DACL is read with SecurityDescriptor::ToSddl,
# which goes through ConvertSecurityDescriptorToStringSecurityDescriptor. That
# call abbreviates the built-in Administrator (RID 500) SID to the alias LA.
# The actual DACL D:AI(A;OICIID;FA;;;LA) is therefore the same ACE as the
# expected …;S-1-5-21-…-500).
-InstallComponentTest.InstalledComponentInheritsDestinationRootAcl
